	{
		id = "terms_shin",
		category = "terms",
		title = "Shin and Mang",
		text = "Shin is a heart held still. It isn't a gift and it doesn't arrive in a moment, the way E.G.O does: it takes years of training and an even temper, and it amplifies what a person already is.\n\nMang is what a trained heart can shape out of that stillness: a ring, burning at the back, made of something the person wants, resents or grieves, held without flinching. Each ring makes every blow heavier. Each ring also nearly doubles the strain on the mind that keeps it. One is hard. Two is rare. The few who carry three are the kind of people the City gives a color to.\n\nNobody had either before the second Light.",
